# What `gcloud builds submit` must not upload.
#
# This file exists because gcloud does NOT read .dockerignore. Without a
# .gcloudignore it synthesises one from .gitignore — which does not exclude
# db/seeds/vectors.parquet, because that file is tracked. The result is a 70 MB
# upload on every build of a file no image reads.
#
# It must stay a superset of the secrecy rules in .dockerignore. Anything
# uploaded here reaches Cloud Build's staging bucket, which is a real place with
# real retention, so `.env` is as load-bearing here as it is there.
#
# `#!include:.dockerignore` is deliberately NOT used: it would make the ignore
# set depend on Docker syntax gcloud parses slightly differently (notably `!`
# re-inclusion), and a difference in interpretation here is a credential in a
# bucket. Two explicit lists, and deploy/README.md says to change both.

# --- secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.local
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.aws/
.gcloud/
service-account*.json

# --- version control ----------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/

# --- the discarded AWS estate -------------------------------------------------
infra/

# --- large data no image reads ------------------------------------------------
db/seeds/vectors.parquet
.pv-objects/
demo/artifacts/

# --- caches and build output --------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.import_linter_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
infra/cdk/cdk.out/

# --- scratch and evidence -----------------------------------------------------
tmp/
.scratch/
.playwright-mcp/
*-report.json
ops/
docs/
evals/
tools/
tests/
**/tests/
Design.pdf
